attribute [local instance 10000] Stacks.Algebraization.modulesHasDerivedCategory

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0A0M], the short exact sequence with the `I`-adic completion of
`H^p(X, ℱ)` in the middle, from the levelwise projection formula; this carries no tag.** Let `A`
be a Noetherian ring, `I ⊆ A` an ideal, `f : X ⟶ Spec A` a Noetherian scheme over `A` and `ℱ` a
coherent `𝒪_X`-module whose cohomology modules `H^p(X, ℱ)` are finite over `A` — the source's
own hypotheses. Write `𝓘 = I · 𝒪_X`. Then for every `p` there is a short exact sequence of
`A`-modules
`0 ⟶ R¹lim H^{p-1}(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ⟶ H^p(X, ℱ)^∧ ⟶ lim H^p(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ⟶ 0`,
the conclusion of the tag.

This is `exists_shortExact_adicCompletion_cohomology` of
`Completion/CohomologyAdicCompletion.lean` with its hypothesis `hBLX` — the identification of
`RΓ(X, lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ)` with the derived `I`-adic completion of `RΓ(X, ℱ)`, which is
[Stacks, Tag 0BLX] — **proved** rather than assumed, from a single named input. Three steps:

* `RΓ(X, lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ)` is a derived limit of `n ↦ RΓ(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ)`, by [Stacks, Tag 0A0K]
  (`isDerivedLimit_single_limit_powerQuotients`) and then [Stacks, Tag 08U1]
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.isDerivedLimit_map_derivedGlobalSectionsOver`);
* the derived `I`-adic completion of `RΓ(X, ℱ)` is a derived limit of
  `n ↦ RΓ(X, ℱ) ⊗^𝐋_A A/Iⁿ`, `A` being Noetherian, by [Stacks, Tag 0EET]
  (`AdicCompletionTor.derivedCompletion_homology_shortExact`), which also produces the reflector,
  so no derived completion functor on `D(A)` is assumed;
* `hproj` identifies the two towers levelwise and compatibly with their transition maps:
  `RΓ(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ≅ RΓ(X, ℱ) ⊗^𝐋_A A/Iⁿ`.

  **`hproj` is false, so this statement is vacuous and is kept only as a record of the
  reduction.** Do not look for a proof of it. Two independent refutations, the first of them
  machine-checked in
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.Completion.LevelwiseProjectionTowerDegeneracy`:
  the two towers are indexed by different exponents, since
  `(adicQuotientSystem I F).obj ⟨0⟩ = ℱ/𝓘⁰ℱ = 0` while the right hand side at `n = 0` is
  `RΓ(X, ℱ) ⊗^𝐋_A A/I`, so `hproj` forces `RΓ(X, ℱ) ⊗^𝐋_A A/I ≅ 0` — already false for
  `X = Spec A`, `ℱ = 𝒪_X` and any proper `I`, where it is `A/I`
  (`isZero_derivedTensor_idealPowerQuotient_zero_of_iso_adicQuotientTower`). And even with the
  exponents aligned it fails: for `A = ℤ`, `I = (p)`, `X = Spec 𝔽ₚ`, `ℱ = 𝒪_X` the left hand
  side is `𝔽ₚ` in degree `0` alone while `𝔽ₚ ⊗^𝐋_ℤ ℤ/pⁿ` carries `Tor₁ = 𝔽ₚ` in degree `-1`.
  The two towers are only **pro**-isomorphic; the `Tor` terms die in the limit, not at any
  finite level, so the honest shape is a map of towers with eventual inverses
  (`NoetherianAdicCompletion.HasEventualInverses`), never a natural isomorphism.

  The genuine inputs to `hBLX` at a general finitely generated `I` are therefore not this, but
  the two gaps recorded in
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/Completion/AdicQuotientDerivedLimit.lean`: the
  projection formula against the Koszul complex at arbitrary `r`, and part (1) of
  [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] at arbitrary `r`. Each is available only for a principal ideal
  (`Stacks.Cohomology.KoszulTowerSections.nonempty_iso_koszulTower_derivedSections`,
  [Stacks, Tag 0H3C]; and
  `Stacks.Cohomology.QuotientTowerFormalFunctions.nonempty_proIso_koszulTower_quotientTower`),
  and [Stacks, Tag 0A0M] is registered at a principal ideal on that basis in
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/Completion/PrincipalCohomologyAdicCompletion.lean`.

Then `Rlim.Pro.nonempty_iso_of_isDerivedLimit_of_natIso` identifies the two sides, and
`CategoryTheory.Adjunction.leftAdjointUniq` moves the identification from the reflector
[Stacks, Tag 0EET] produces to an arbitrary one, which is the form `hBLX` is stated in.

**No part of [Stacks, Tags 099E or 099F] is a hypothesis here**, which is worth recording
because the other statements of this file once carried Tag 099F, which they no longer do; here
the left hand side of `hBLX` is the *formal* completion `lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ` and not a reflector applied
to anything, and the reflector on
`D(A)` comes from [Stacks, Tag 0920]. The single assumed input is `hproj`. It carries no tag all
the same, because `hproj` is a result the source's proof invokes rather than one of its
hypotheses.

Not covered: the properness clause, the vanishing of the `R¹lim` term for a proper `f`. It rests
on the Mittag-Leffler condition of [Stacks, Tag 02OB], which is not in this library; the proper
mapping theorem [Stacks, Tag 02O5] below that is available, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProperCoherenceWitness.higherDirectImageIsCoherent`.

This statement lives in this file rather than beside its engine because
`Completion/CohomologyAdicCompletion.lean` follows a different route to the same tag —
[Stacks, Tag 0BLD] at a principal ideal. -/
theorem exists_shortExact_adicCompletion_cohomology_of_isDerivedLimit
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A)
    {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsNoetherian X] (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A))
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsCoherent]
    (hfinite : ∀ p : ℤ, Module.Finite A
      ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) p).obj
        ((derivedGlobalSectionsOver f).obj
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0).obj F))))
    (hproj : ((adicQuotientSystem
          (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf A I f) F ⋙
        DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0) ⋙ derivedGlobalSectionsOver f) ≅
      NoetherianAdicCompletion.idealPowerQuotientSystem I ⋙
        (CochainComplex.DerivedTensor.canonicalDerivedTensorProduct A).tensor.obj
          ((derivedGlobalSectionsOver f).obj
            ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0).obj F)))
    (p : ℤ) :
    let T : ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) :=
      adicQuotientSystem (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf A I f) F ⋙
        DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0 ⋙ derivedGlobalSectionsOver f
    let H : ℤ → DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} A := fun q ↦
      DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) q
    ∃ (i : CompletionSequences.firstDerivedLimit A (T ⋙ H (p - 1)) ⟶
        ModuleCat.of A (AdicCompletion I
          ((H p).obj ((derivedGlobalSectionsOver f).obj
            ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0).obj F)))))
      (q : ModuleCat.of A (AdicCompletion I
          ((H p).obj ((derivedGlobalSectionsOver f).obj
            ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0).obj F)))) ⟶
        limit (T ⋙ H p))
      (w : i ≫ q = 0),
      (ShortComplex.mk i q w).ShortExact := by
  have hprods : HasProductsOfShape ℕ (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) :=
    Stacks.DerivedProducts.hasProductsOfShape_derivedCategory
  set single := DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0 with hsingle
  set S := adicQuotientSystem (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf A I f) F with hS
  -- [Stacks, Tag 0EET]: the reflector on `D(A)`, and its ideal-power derived-limit presentation.
  obtain ⟨L, ⟨adjL⟩, hlimL, -, -⟩ :=
    AdicCompletionTor.derivedCompletion_homology_shortExact A I
      (CochainComplex.DerivedTensor.canonicalDerivedTensorProduct A)
  -- [Stacks, Tag 0A0K]: the formal completion is the derived limit of the adic quotient tower.
  obtain ⟨hprodSheaf, hlimSheaf⟩ :=
    isDerivedLimit_single_limit_powerQuotients
      (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf A I f) F
  have hprodSheaf' : HasProduct fun n : ℕ ↦ (S ⋙ single).obj ⟨n⟩ := hprodSheaf
  have hlimSheaf' : IsDerivedLimit (S ⋙ single) (single.obj (limit S)) := hlimSheaf
  -- [Stacks, Tag 08U1]: derived global sections carry that to a derived limit in `D(A)`.
  refine exists_shortExact_adicCompletion_cohomology_of_forall_reflector A I f F hfinite
    (fun C adj ↦ ?_) p
  -- [Stacks, Tag 0H9L] at `hproj`: the two derived limits agree, which is [Stacks, Tag 0BLX].
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := Rlim.Pro.nonempty_iso_of_exists_isDerivedLimit_of_natIso
    (isDerivedLimit_map_derivedGlobalSectionsOver f (S ⋙ single) (single.obj (limit S)) hlimSheaf')
    (hlimL ((derivedGlobalSectionsOver f).obj (single.obj F))) hproj
  -- Left adjoints are unique, so the identification holds at every reflector.
  exact ⟨((ObjectProperty.ι (show ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) from
      fun K ↦ IsDerivedComplete I K)).mapIso
      ((adjL.leftAdjointUniq adj).app
        ((derivedGlobalSectionsOver f).obj (single.obj F)))).symm ≪≫ e.symm⟩

end Stacks.Algebraization

